{"availability":"available","full":"StellarHyperion/stellarhyperion-frontend","name":"stellarhyperion-frontend","description":"Web interface for Hyperion, enabling cross-chain routing, live quotes, wallet connectivity, and transfer tracking.","category":"Other","language":"TypeScript","stars":148,"forks":143,"created":"2026-09-26T11:07:14Z","updated":"2026-10-12T21:55:40Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://stellarhyperion.vercel.app/","topics":["cross-chain","nextjs","react","soroban","stellar","typescript","viem","wagmi","web3"],"demo":"https://stellarhyperion.vercel.app/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-16T02:46:35.844Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-16T02:46:35.844Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-16T02:46:35.844Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T09:08:26.196Z","stars":148,"forks":143},{"at":"2026-10-16T02:46:35.844Z","stars":148,"forks":143}],"technologies":["React","Next.js"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["The front end for a router that moves money between Stellar and the EVM chains.","The product's claim is narrow and specific: Hyperion never decides for itself that a cross-chain message is real. It prices four rails that already made that decision and were audited for it, takes the one that lands the most money, and tells you what the other three would have cost. The whole design of this app exists to make that claim checkable rather than just stated, which is why the centrepiece is a diagram of four rails with the losers still drawn and their reasons attached."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/StellarHyperion/stellarhyperion-frontend/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"f26e56e40b2dc9a4b320d11326f9cd8cefd42311adef9d540d15fdecbb1bf6b9","extractedAt":"2026-10-10T09:08:26.375Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T09:08:26.375Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"The front end for a router that moves money between Stellar and the EVM chains.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/StellarHyperion/ste